{
 "_README": "#631 — Epic (ML 20) Lunar/Solar gems the upstream gear-planner crafting dump does not carry. ADDITIVE ONLY: an entry whose name already exists in the pool is a build failure, never a silent overwrite — this shard may not correct upstream, only fill a hole it leaves.",
 "_why": "The wiki's Lunar Gem page lists 103 gem families at three tiers; upstream carries 103 Heroic and 103 Legendary but only 17 Epic, and current master (checked 2026-08-30) still carries 17. So a refresh does not fix it. Epic gems arrived with Update 73 (Tavern Tales) per the wiki; upstream appears simply not to have scraped that tier.",
 "_method": "The VALUE comes from the wiki's Epic column. The affix NAMES and BONUS TYPES come from our own shipped Heroic record for the same gem, NOT from the wiki row — the row's type text proved unreliable (it reads 'Profane' where the ruled type is 'Profane Natural', and mis-assigns across adjacent rows), while the (affix, type) shape is constant across tiers for all 103 bases, measured. Parse validated against the 204 shipped Heroic/Legendary records: 203 matched exactly.",
 "_stale_guard": "Each entry records the sibling record it was derived from. The build FAILS when that sibling's affixes no longer match, rather than pinning a derived Epic value over a source that moved.",
 "_excluded": {
  "Lunar Gem of Weapon Damage": "the wiki's Heroic value (2) disagrees with the shipped Heroic record (Deadly Profane 1), so this gem's row failed the cross-check that validates every other Epic value. Its Epic value is therefore unverified and the gem is deliberately NOT added. Resolve the Heroic discrepancy first."
 },
